Implement function solve(input). Input is an array of lessons with subject, predicate, value, scope (string), and type. Exclude intuition, hypothesis and disputed lessons. Among remaining lessons, exclude every non-negative lesson if another remaining non-negative lesson has the same subject, predicate and scope but a different value (JSON primitive). Keep negative lessons, which do not create conflicts. Preserve the input order and return the accepted original lesson objects. Do not mutate input. Return only JavaScript function solve(input); no imports, exports or prose.

Current implementation:
function solve(input) { return input.filter(l => !['intuition','hypothesis','disputed'].includes(l.type)); }

